From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-08-18
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] basicswap: make the per-coin pid wait configurable

initialiseDaemon()'s post-start handshake polls for the daemon's pid file 20
times at 0.5s intervals -- a hard 10 second budget -- and raises if the pid is
still unreadable. On Windows, with three coin daemons (particld, litecoind,
monerod) coming up concurrently against Defender's on-access scanner and a cold
page cache, the pid file routinely lands later than that, and the run aborts
with a spurious "Failed to get daemon pid" even though every daemon is healthy
and finishes starting seconds later.

Read the iteration count from the BSX_PID_WAIT_ITERS environment variable,
defaulting to the existing literal 20. With the variable unset the behaviour is
byte-for-byte upstream's, so this is a no-op for every current deployment; the
Windows supervisor sets BSX_PID_WAIT_ITERS=40 (20s) or higher.

Deliberately NOT a raised constant: the right budget is a property of the host
(disk speed, AV, how many daemons start at once), not of the software, so it
belongs in the environment rather than in a new upstream default.

Upstream-PR candidate (not yet submitted).

Applies to: basicswap v0.18.7 (079a0d43ed16590eecda2f3d6a3481f847360175)
Marker in patched source: PWNDA-PATCH-2
---
 basicswap/basicswap.py | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/basicswap/basicswap.py b/basicswap/basicswap.py
index 989c1fe..eed04a8 100644
--- a/basicswap/basicswap.py
+++ b/basicswap/basicswap.py
@@ -1273,7 +1273,11 @@ class BasicSwap(BaseApp, BSXNetwork, UIApp):
             # Wait for daemon to start
             # Test pids to ensure authcookie is read for the correct process
             datadir_pid = -1
-            for i in range(20):
+            # PWNDA-PATCH-2: Windows daemons write pid files slower under multi-daemon
+            # startup contention; make the 10s (20*0.5s) wait configurable. Absent env
+            # var == upstream default of 20, so this is a no-op for upstream.
+            _pwnda_pid_iters = int(os.getenv("BSX_PID_WAIT_ITERS", "20"))
+            for i in range(_pwnda_pid_iters):
                 try:
                     if os.name == "nt" and cc["core_version_group"] <= 17:
                         # Older core versions don't write a pid file on windows
